acpipci_intr_swizzle() indexes pa_bridgeih[swizpin - 1] where
swizpin = PPB_INTERRUPT_SWIZZLE(pa_rawintrpin, dev) = (((pin + dev - 1) % 4) + 1).
A downstream/hotplug PCIe bridge whose config Interrupt Pin register reads 0
(PCI_INTERRUPT_PIN_NONE) at device 0 yields swizpin 0, so the access reads
pa_bridgeih[-1] - the 32 bytes immediately before the parent bridge's sc_ih[4],
i.e. its {dv_parent, sc_tag} - producing a bogus pci_intr_handle (ih_pc = the
parent bus's pci_softc, ih_dmat = a pcitag, ih_type = a nonzero fragment).
acpipci_intr_establish then sees ih_type != PCI_INTX, routes into the MSI path,
and dereferences ih_pc as a chipset - panic (PC-align / bad load).

This bites AWS Graviton4/5 (c8g/c9g): the third bridge down a hotplug ppb chain
(ppb0->pci2->ppb1->pci3->ppb2) is the only one with Slot-Implemented set, a
non-NULL pa_bridgeih (depth >= 2), rawintrpin 0, and no usable MSI cap, so it
alone runs the swizzle fallback and hits the -1 index; it panics attaching that
bridge, before ENA (on a deeper root) is ever reached. c7g (flat, no chain)
never runs this path. A function with no interrupt pin has nothing to swizzle -
bail before computing swizpin. Present in 7.9 and -current; upstreamable.

--- sys/arch/arm64/dev/acpipci.c
+++ sys/arch/arm64/dev/acpipci.c
@@ -463,6 +463,14 @@
 	pcireg_t id;
 
 	if (pa->pa_bridgeih == NULL)
+		return -1;
+
+	/*
+	 * A function with no interrupt pin has nothing to swizzle; bail
+	 * before PPB_INTERRUPT_SWIZZLE() turns pin 0 into swizpin 0 and the
+	 * pa_bridgeih[swizpin - 1] access below reads out of bounds.
+	 */
+	if (pa->pa_rawintrpin == PCI_INTERRUPT_PIN_NONE)
 		return -1;
 
 	pci_decompose_tag(pa->pa_pc, pa->pa_tag, NULL, &dev, NULL);
